      "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR optimizes the CUDA  kernel () by vectorizing the output store operation.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe kernel previously wrote each thread's 8 dequantized half-precision values as 8 separate scalar 2-byte stores, despite already holding them in a  register.\n\n## Solution\n\nReplace 8 scalar stores with a single 16-byte  store. The math is unchanged and output is bitwise identical.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Removed the unused  shared memory array and  pointer\n- Replaced the loop of 8 scalar stores with a single  store\n\n## Performance Results (H100)\n\n| Layer (K × N) | Before | After | Speedup |\n|---------------|--------|-------|---------|\n| qkv_proj (4096 × 6144) | 112.7 µs | 31.7 µs | 3.56× |\n| o_proj (4096 × 4096) | 52.8 µs | 21.7 µs | 2.44× |\n| gate_up_proj (4096 × 28672) | 518.3 µs | 141.6 µs | 3.66× |\n| down_proj (14336 × 4096) | 175.7 µs | 71.6 µs | 2.45× |\n\n## End-to-End Impact (VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1)\n\n- TPOT at concurrency 1: **34.9 → 16.0 ms** (2.19× faster)\n- Output throughput at concurrency 32: **762 → 1407 tok/s** (1.85× higher)\n- GSM8K accuracy, greedy outputs, logprobs: **identical**\n\n## Validation\n\n- 377 tests pass (`test_awq.py`, `test_awq_triton.py`)\n- New `test_awq_dequantize` validates CUDA op against PyTorch reference with exact equality (`atol=0, rtol=0`)\n- Bitwise equality verified with `torch.equal` on all four layer shapes\n- Default Machete path unchanged (control test)\n\nFixes #63590",
      "changedFiles": 2,
